s, 1951 to 2025, on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids. September to October and November to December each came in under 90% of normal in 38 of those years, the most of any pair. In 2025, February to March ran 53% of normal and September to October 59%, while July to August hit 126%. Every grid had its driest year in 2005, and grid 15431 fell to 48% that year.</p>"}
